From: Greg Bowser <topnotcher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Oct 2013 23:46:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mpc: fix a logic error that prevented pkts from sending

Fixes an issue that begin with 4cf1605299c06df111acf15cf2e94eb2d52cc562,
where the mpc master would not transmit any messages.

diff --git a/include/mpc.c b/include/mpc.c
index b2fa669..07b32e7 100644
--- a/include/mpc.c
+++ b/include/mpc.c
@@ -358,8 +358,8 @@ static inline void mpc_master_run(void) {
 	ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) {
 		if ( queue_empty(&tx_state.queue.hdr) || tx_state.status != TX_STATUS_IDLE ) 
 			okay = 0; 
-
-		tx_state.status = TX_STATUS_BUSY;
+		else 
+			tx_state.status = TX_STATUS_BUSY;
 	}

 	if (!okay) return;
-- 
2.25.1

Based on the commit message, the root cause and the patch provided below, you need to:

1. explain how the bug occurs, including all code statements that are most likely to lead to the bug and why. 
2. explain how the bug is fixed, including code statements fixing the bug and why. 

You must include one or more code statements in point 1 and 2.
Code statements included in point 1 should be as brief as possible, only include the ones that are most related to the root cause and  the number of code statements may not exceed 3.


Here is the commit message:
mpc: fix a logic error that prevented pkts from sending

Fixes an issue that begin with 4cf1605299c06df111acf15cf2e94eb2d52cc562,
where the mpc master would not transmit any messages.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a logic error in the `mpc_master_run` function, where the status of the transmission was incorrectly set to `TX_STATUS_BUSY` regardless of whether the transmission queue was empty or the status was not idle. This prevented the master from transmitting any messages, as the status was not updated correctly based on the conditions of the queue and status.

Here is the patch:
  */
 static inline void mpc_master_run(void) { 

 	uint8_t okay = 1;

 	ATOMIC_BLOCK(ATOMIC_RESTORESTATE) {
 		if ( queue_empty(&tx_state.queue.hdr) || tx_state.status != TX_STATUS_IDLE ) 
 			okay = 0; 
-
-		tx_state.status = TX_STATUS_BUSY;
+		else 
+			tx_state.status = TX_STATUS_BUSY;
 	}

 	if (!okay) return;

 	mpc_pkt * pkt = &tx_state.queue.items[ tx_state.queue.hdr.read ].pkt;
 	tx_state.pkt = pkt;
 	tx_state.len = sizeof(*pkt) + pkt->len;
 	tx_state.byte = 0;

 	MPC_TWI.MASTER.ADDR = tx_state.queue.items[ tx_state.queue.hdr.read ].addr<<1 | 0;
 	queue_rd_idx(&tx_state.queue.hdr);
 }



